{
 "about": "The one-time move into ~/.benji from ~/.chilly, ~/chilly or ~/pal, as cases both sides must agree on: benji/home.py (selftest_home.py) and BenjiCore/HomeMigration.swift (HomeMigrationTests.swift). Each case builds a throwaway home folder from `before` (`dirs`, `files` as path: text, `links` as path: target relative to the home), optionally sets BENJI_WORKDIR (`workdir_env`), runs the move once (or `runs` times), and checks `kind` of the FIRST run, whether a notice was given, the paths that must `exist` or be `absent` afterwards, the marker's kind, and that ~/.benji is mode 700 when the move made it. `python_only` cases are for the engine alone (the app does not know the folder from before the rename, ~/pal).",
